OL,3,ATrainline, Virgin Atlantic and RED
OL,4,ADriving School investigated over 'drip
OL,5,Apricing'
OL,6,
OL,7,FTrainline, Virgin Atlantic and RED
OL,8,FDriving School are being investigated
OL,9,Fby the consumer watchdog over concerns
OL,10,Fthey are not showing full prices
OL,11,Fupfront to customers.
OL,13,FThe Competition and Markets Authority
OL,14,F(CMA) is examining whether the three
OL,15,Fcompanies engaged in so-called 'drip
OL,16,Fpricing', which is an illegal practice
OL,17,Fwhere mandatory fees are not included
OL,18,Fin the headline price shown to
OL,19,Fcustomers.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,0,100
